1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
 Alrighty. So, in our last video, we learned about the basics of using Visual Studio Code,

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
 and we also set up our template project. In this one, we're going to be looking at installing

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
 extensions within Visual Studio Code that is going to add some very useful functionality.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
 Alright, so let's dive in.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
 We can see that I have Visual Studio Code opened here in our template folder,

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
 and on the right side, we have our HTML file of our template.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000
 And if you recall, when I click on this icon here,

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
 it opens up the Explorer that shows the files within our folder.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
 And if we go down to the bottom here, these blocks,

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,000
 if we click on this, this opens up our extensions pane.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,000
 So you can see that there are some popular extensions here for Python, C++,

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
 things like that, and it also has some recommended ones down here.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
 I'm going to just minimize these for now.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
 And you can see that we have zero installed extensions currently.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
 So, we're going to change that, and we're going to install a few of them.

16
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,000
 So, I'm going to start with a few different ones here.

17
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
 First one is going to be called Color Highlight.

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
 And you can see that it's the first option here.

19
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
 And if we click on it, it gives us some information about it.

20
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
 But basically, this thumbnail here tells you all you need to know.

21
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
 Essentially, it is going to highlight the hex code

22
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
 or whatever color value that you have in the actual color that it is.

23
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,000
 So, I find this really useful because I don't memorize what all of the hex codes are.

24
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,000
 There's, you know, 14 million combinations of hex codes.

25
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,000
 So, this is a great way to actually see what the color is.

26
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
 So, we're going to go ahead and click Install.

27
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
 Okay, great. You can see that. It's installed.

28
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
 And we're going to go on to a couple more.

29
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
 We're going to test them all out at the end.

30
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:17,000
 So, the next one I'm going to suggest is IntelliSense for CSS.

31
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,000
 And we can see, yes, it's this one here.

32
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
 It's for CSS class names.

33
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:28,000
 And you can see that it actually has a little video down here.

34
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:35,000
 But basically, what this is doing is, it is taking any classes that exist in a style sheet

35
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
 that is linked to the HTML.

36
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,000
 And then, basically, it adds a way to auto-complete

37
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
 and use a class that is already existing,

38
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
 that is being referenced from our HTML.

39
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
 So, that is very handy.

40
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
 We'll test that out in a moment.

41
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
 Okay, that one's installed.

42
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:02,000
 Next, we're going to add another extension called CSS Peak.

43
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
 Okay, great.

44
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:11,000
 And this one allows us to enter HTML document to hover over a certain class.

45
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
 So, let's say I have this class called comments.

46
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:19,000
 It's going to allow me to hover over and actually have a little preview.

47
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
 You can see like this rectangle here.

48
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:26,000
 A little preview of what the styling actually is for that style class.

49
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
 And it also allows you to jump over to it.

50
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:36,000
 But for me, just being able to peek and see what the properties of the CSS class are is very helpful like this.

51
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:41,000
 Okay, so we're going to install that as well.

52
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
 Okay, great. That one's installed.

53
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,000
 And we will install a few more extensions later on in the course.

54
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
 But the last very, very important one.

55
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:57,000
 And I think the absolute most useful extension is going to be live server.

56
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:01,000
 So, you can see it has 39.5 million downloads.

57
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:07,000
 So, we're going to click on that and we're going to install this.

58
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,000
 So, what this allows us to do, you can actually scroll down and see.

59
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
 And we kind of have a similar setup here.

60
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:19,000
 So, at the very bottom of the page, it's going to have an option that's going to say go live.

61
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
 Yeah, you can see it's right there.

62
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:27,000
 And basically, what this is going to do in combination with the auto save that we already have turned on,

63
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:34,000
 it's going to in real time update our HTML file without us having to actually press the refresh button.

64
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
 So, that is very, very helpful.

65
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,000
 Okay, so those are our extensions.

66
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:46,000
 We're going to start by testing out our live server extension first.

67
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:51,000
 Because that to me is the most important of the ones that we've installed.

68
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:58,000
 So, I'm just going to go ahead, make sure that you are on the HTML file. It will not work unless you're actually on that file.

69
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:02,000
 And we're going to go down to the bottom and we're just going to click go live.

70
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:13,000
 And you can see that it loaded another tab and the address is 127001 and port 5500.

71
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:19,000
 So, that is using a local host server to actually serve our static web page.

72
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,000
 So, I can go ahead and close the existing one.

73
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:28,000
 And now, if I make a change, so let's say I change the title to testing.

74
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
 You'll see that it automatically refreshes.

75
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
 I didn't need to refresh the page.

76
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
 And because I have auto save enabled in Visual Studio Code,

77
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:43,000
 it is just basically changing by magic, which is very, very nice.

78
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:47,000
 Okay, so let's add some content now to our page.

79
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:52,000
 So, first we're going to add an h1.test press enter.

80
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:56,000
 So, it's going to create our h1 element with our class of test.

81
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,000
 And we're going to type hello world.

82
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:04,000
 And then below that, we're going to create an i element.

83
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:09,000
 And we're going to show off the IntelliSense extension.

84
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:15,000
 So, this is going to work because we are linking to this font awesome style sheet.

85
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:20,000
 And it's going to automatically pick up all of those classes.

86
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
 So, if I go ahead and I add the class attribute.

87
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
 So, we're going to start with fa.

88
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
 And you can see it's there at the top.

89
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
 That's the first one we need to add an icon.

90
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
 And then from there, I can actually search.

91
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
 So, let's say that I wanted a star icon.

92
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
 I can actually just type star.

93
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:41,000
 And you'll see that it has all the options that have star within it.

94
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
 And we'll go ahead, just click on the first one.

95
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
 And you can see here that we have our star icon.

96
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
 Okay, so that's how the IntelliSense works.

97
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,000
 That's very nice.

98
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:57,000
 Next, let's go ahead and actually create our test class here.

99
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:02,000
 So, in our CSS, we're going to create our class.test.

100
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:07,000
 And we will use a color to show off our color highlight here.

101
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,000
 So, let's add a color Dodger blue.

102
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:15,000
 And you can see that the whole text is now Dodger blue.

103
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:20,000
 And I can do a similar thing with a hex code.

104
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,000
 So, let's say that I just did 00, 00, 00.

105
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
 And that's black.

106
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
 And you can see that it automatically colors it black.

107
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:34,000
 And I also have the option when I hover over the color that I can use a very handy color figure.

108
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
 So, I can do that.

109
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
 And then I let it go.

110
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:43,000
 And you can see that the text again becomes highlighted in that color.

111
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
 So, that is very useful.

112
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
 So, we'll get rid of that for now.

113
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:52,000
 Let's say that we want to also maybe add a margin back to this.

114
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
 So, let's say we're going to add a margin of 10 pixels as well.

115
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
 Okay.

116
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:01,000
 And if we go back now, so that's our color highlight extension in action.

117
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
 Okay, so we're going to go back to our HTML document here.

118
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,000
 And we're going to test our last extension.

119
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
 And this is our CSS peak extension.

120
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:14,000
 So, on a Mac, you're going to hold down the command key.

121
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
 On Windows, you would hold down the control key.

122
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:20,000
 And then you're just going to hover over the class name.

123
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
 So, I'm going to go ahead and hold down command.

124
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
 And then I'm going to hover over test.

125
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
 And you can see, very, very cool.

126
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
 We have our popover window.

127
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:34,000
 And it shows us the values within our test class.

128
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,000
 Okay.

129
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
 That is awesome.

130
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
 All right.

